    "def-td-regular-hamiltonian-shell-preparation": {
      "citations": [],
      "derivations": [],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Fix an integer $n\\ge1$, a canonical chart with physical coordinates $q_i$ in metres and $p_i$ in $\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}}$, and the corresponding dimensionless coordinates $\\hat q_i=q_i/(1\\,\\mathrm m)$ and $\\hat p_i=p_i/(1\\,\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}})$. Boundary empty: The statement explicitly requires a nonempty state set, nonzero sector, nonempty shell, or positive trace; no empty-model conclusion is claimed.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Definition",
            "source_excerpt": "Fix an integer $n\\ge1$, a canonical chart with physical coordinates $q_i$ in metres and $p_i$ in $\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}}$, and the corresponding dimensionless coordinates $\\hat q_i=q_i/(1\\,\\mathrm m)$ and $\\hat p_i=p_i/(1\\,\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}})$. Let $O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{2n}$ be the open domain of the numerical vector $\\hat x=(\\hat q,\\hat p)$, let $\\hat H:O\\to\\mathbb R$ be the numerical energy map with physical energy $H=(1\\,\\mathrm J)\\hat H$, and require $\\hat H$ to have continuous partial derivatives through order two. A specified open interval $J_E\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ is a regular compact-shell band when $\\hat H^{-1}(K)$ is compact in $O$ for every compact $K\\subset J_E$ and $\\nabla\\hat H$ is nonzero at every point of $\\hat H^{-1}(J_E)$.\n\nFor $\\hat E\\in J_E$, the energy shell is $\\Sigma_{\\hat E}:=\\{x\\in O:\\hat H(x)=\\hat E\\}$. The graph-chart definition of the weighted shell integral is [[def-tdmath-regular-energy-shell]]: in a local graph chart $x_i=h(z,\\hat E)$, its coarea measure is $d\\mu_{\\hat E}=dA_{\\hat E}/|\\nabla\\hat H|$, with graph-area factor and gradient in the dimensionless Euclidean coordinates. Set $D(\\hat E):=\\int_{\\Sigma_{\\hat E}}d\\mu_{\\hat E}$ and admit the preparation only when $\\Sigma_{\\hat E}\\ne\\varnothing$ and $0<D(\\hat E)<\\infty$. Its normalized shell law is $\\nu_{\\hat E}(A):=D(\\hat E)^{-1}\\mu_{\\hat E}(A\\cap\\Sigma_{\\hat E})$. The current draft theorem [[thm-tdmath-regular-energy-shell-measure]] proves the coarea identity, chart independence and positive finite shell mass under its stated $C^2$, compact-regular-band hypotheses; its statement and proof are present, while its acceptance remains unresolved. Multiplying the unnormalized shell measure by a fixed positive phase-volume normalization does not change $\\nu_{\\hat E}$.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "e97f23b23076b1850ab0ea75c34a646b748d94a916a204541916ddb704132453",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
        {
          "case": "zero",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Statement/Example scope: Fix an integer $n\\ge1$, a canonical chart with physical coordinates $q_i$ in metres and $p_i$ in $\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}}$, and the corresponding dimensionless coordinates $\\hat q_i=q_i/(1\\,\\mathrm m)$ and $\\hat p_i=p_i/(1\\,\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}})$. Case zero: Zero-energy levels are admitted where the model allows them and contribute weight e^0=1; positive-temperature assumptions exclude a zero-temperature limit (Statement).",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Definition",
            "source_excerpt": "Fix an integer $n\\ge1$, a canonical chart with physical coordinates $q_i$ in metres and $p_i$ in $\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}}$, and the corresponding dimensionless coordinates $\\hat q_i=q_i/(1\\,\\mathrm m)$ and $\\hat p_i=p_i/(1\\,\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}})$. Let $O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{2n}$ be the open domain of the numerical vector $\\hat x=(\\hat q,\\hat p)$, let $\\hat H:O\\to\\mathbb R$ be the numerical energy map with physical energy $H=(1\\,\\mathrm J)\\hat H$, and require $\\hat H$ to have continuous partial derivatives through order two. A specified open interval $J_E\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ is a regular compact-shell band when $\\hat H^{-1}(K)$ is compact in $O$ for every compact $K\\subset J_E$ and $\\nabla\\hat H$ is nonzero at every point of $\\hat H^{-1}(J_E)$.\n\nFor $\\hat E\\in J_E$, the energy shell is $\\Sigma_{\\hat E}:=\\{x\\in O:\\hat H(x)=\\hat E\\}$. The graph-chart definition of the weighted shell integral is [[def-tdmath-regular-energy-shell]]: in a local graph chart $x_i=h(z,\\hat E)$, its coarea measure is $d\\mu_{\\hat E}=dA_{\\hat E}/|\\nabla\\hat H|$, with graph-area factor and gradient in the dimensionless Euclidean coordinates. Set $D(\\hat E):=\\int_{\\Sigma_{\\hat E}}d\\mu_{\\hat E}$ and admit the preparation only when $\\Sigma_{\\hat E}\\ne\\varnothing$ and $0<D(\\hat E)<\\infty$. Its normalized shell law is $\\nu_{\\hat E}(A):=D(\\hat E)^{-1}\\mu_{\\hat E}(A\\cap\\Sigma_{\\hat E})$. The current draft theorem [[thm-tdmath-regular-energy-shell-measure]] proves the coarea identity, chart independence and positive finite shell mass under its stated $C^2$, compact-regular-band hypotheses; its statement and proof are present, while its acceptance remains unresolved. Multiplying the unnormalized shell measure by a fixed positive phase-volume normalization does not change $\\nu_{\\hat E}$.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "e97f23b23076b1850ab0ea75c34a646b748d94a916a204541916ddb704132453",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
        {
          "case": "one",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Fix an integer $n\\ge1$, a canonical chart with physical coordinates $q_i$ in metres and $p_i$ in $\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}}$, and the corresponding dimensionless coordinates $\\hat q_i=q_i/(1\\,\\mathrm m)$ and $\\hat p_i=p_i/(1\\,\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}})$. Boundary one: The claim concerns a countable/multidimensional, geometric, pressure-limit, or multi-site branch; a one-state case is outside the declared object class.",
          "case_scope": {
