          "case": "endpoints",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Let $I$ be a specified nonempty countable microstate list with energies $E_i$ in joules, counted once, and let $J_\\beta\\subset(0,\\infty)$ be open. Boundary endpoints: The claims use positive/open parameter domains or a stated limit; no excluded endpoint value is evaluated or inferred.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $I$ be a specified nonempty countable microstate list with energies $E_i$ in joules, counted once, and let $J_\\beta\\subset(0,\\infty)$ be open. For $\\beta\\in J_\\beta$, define $Z(\\beta)=\\sum_i e^{-\\beta E_i}$ and, when $0<Z(\\beta)<\\infty$, $p_i(\\beta)=e^{-\\beta E_i}/Z(\\beta)$. Suppose every compact interval $K\\subset J_\\beta$ admits a summable sequence $a_i\\ge0$ with $(1+|E_i|^2)e^{-\\beta E_i}\\le a_i$ for all $i$ and $\\beta\\in K$. Then $Z$ is $C^2$, $-\\partial_\\beta\\log Z=\\bar E_\\beta$, $\\partial_\\beta^2\\log Z=\\operatorname{Var}_\\beta(E)$, and the dimensionless Gibbs entropy is finite with\n$$-\\sum_i p_i\\log p_i=\\log Z+\\beta\\bar E_\\beta.$$\nThus $F_{\\mathrm{stat}}=-k_{\\mathrm B}T\\log Z=\\bar E_\\beta-TS_\\beta$ for $\\beta=(k_{\\mathrm B}T)^{-1}$. A lower bound on the energies alone does not supply the summable envelope or finite partition function.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "6560f1c1bfdbfe5c050e2f34b8e9abe7876ea29e89d4974e43195f54cf668ea6",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
        {
          "case": "nonempty-choice",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Statement/Example scope: Let $I$ be a specified nonempty countable microstate list with energies $E_i$ in joules, counted once, and let $J_\\beta\\subset(0,\\infty)$ be open. Case nonempty-choice: The statement supplies the required nonempty finite set, nonzero sector, nonempty shell, complete basis, or explicit countable model; normalization is checked in step 1.1 where present.",
          "case_scope": {
