          "reason": "Let $(\\Omega,\\epsilon)$ be a finite nonempty microstate model, let $T>0$, and let $q_x=e^{-\\beta E_x}/Z$ be its canonical probabilities at $\\beta=(k_{\\mathrm B}T)^{-1}$. Boundary endpoints: The claims use positive/open parameter domains or a stated limit; no excluded endpoint value is evaluated or inferred.",
          "case_scope": {
