            "source_excerpt": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice and the canonical Gibbs-preparation assumption [[post-nrqm-many-body-canonical-equilibrium-ensemble]]. Restrict to its $G=H$ branch: the declared energy operator $H$ is self-adjoint, bounded below, and measured in joules; $T>0$ is in kelvins, $\\beta=(k_{\\mathrm B}T)^{-1}$ is in $\\mathrm{J^{-1}}$, and $K_\\beta=e^{-\\beta H}$ has $0<Z_\\beta=\\operatorname{Tr}K_\\beta<\\infty$. Suppose also that on an open interval $J_\\beta\\subset(0,\\infty)$ containing $\\beta$, every compact $C\\subset J_\\beta$ admits a summable family $a_j\\ge0$ with $(1+|E_j|^2)e^{-\\gamma E_j}\\le a_j$ for all energy eigenvalues $E_j$ and $\\gamma\\in C$. For the adopted density $\\rho_\\beta=K_\\beta/Z_\\beta$, the mean and variance of $H$ are finite and\n$$-\\partial_\\beta\\log Z_\\beta=\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho_\\beta H),\\qquad \\partial_\\beta^2\\log Z_\\beta=\\operatorname{Var}_{\\rho_\\beta}(H),\\qquad S_{\\mathrm{vN}}(\\rho_\\beta)=k_{\\mathrm B}\\bigl(\\log Z_\\beta+\\beta\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho_\\beta H)\\bigr).$$\nThus $F_{\\mathrm{stat}}=-k_{\\mathrm B}T\\log Z_\\beta=\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho_\\beta H)-T S_{\\mathrm{vN}}(\\rho_\\beta)$. This statement does not extend the Helmholtz interpretation to an effective generator $H-\\mu\\mathcal N$.",
