    "pthm-td-invariant-regular-microcanonical-shell": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-td-regular-hamiltonian-shell-preparation",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix an integer $n\\ge1$, a canonical chart with physical coordinates $q_i$ in metres and $p_i$ in $\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}}$, and the corresponding dimensionless coordinates $\\hat q_i=q_i/(1\\,\\mathrm m)$ and $\\hat p_i=p_i/(1\\,\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}})$. Let $O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{2n}$ be the open domain of the numerical vector $\\hat x=(\\hat q,\\hat p)$, let $\\hat H:O\\to\\mathbb R$ be the numerical energy map with physical energy $H=(1\\,\\mathrm J)\\hat H$, and require $\\hat H$ to have continuous partial derivatives through order two. A specified open interval $J_E\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ is a regular compact-shell band when $\\hat H^{-1}(K)$ is compact in $O$ for every compact $K\\subset J_E$ and $\\nabla\\hat H$ is nonzero at every point of $\\hat H^{-1}(J_E)$.\n\nFor $\\hat E\\in J_E$, the energy shell is $\\Sigma_{\\hat E}:=\\{x\\in O:\\hat H(x)=\\hat E\\}$. The graph-chart definition of the weighted shell integral is [[def-tdmath-regular-energy-shell]]: in a local graph chart $x_i=h(z,\\hat E)$, its coarea measure is $d\\mu_{\\hat E}=dA_{\\hat E}/|\\nabla\\hat H|$, with graph-area factor and gradient in the dimensionless Euclidean coordinates. Set $D(\\hat E):=\\int_{\\Sigma_{\\hat E}}d\\mu_{\\hat E}$ and admit the preparation only when $\\Sigma_{\\hat E}\\ne\\varnothing$ and $0<D(\\hat E)<\\infty$. Its normalized shell law is $\\nu_{\\hat E}(A):=D(\\hat E)^{-1}\\mu_{\\hat E}(A\\cap\\Sigma_{\\hat E})$. The current draft theorem [[thm-tdmath-regular-energy-shell-measure]] proves the coarea identity, chart independence and positive finite shell mass under its stated $C^2$, compact-regular-band hypotheses; its statement and proof are present, while its acceptance remains unresolved. Multiplying the unnormalized shell measure by a fixed positive phase-volume normalization does not change $\\nu_{\\hat E}$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "post-td-microcanonical-sampling",
          "source_section": "Postulate",
          "quote": "For a finite microstate model and a declared energy value $E_0$ in joules and resolution $\\delta\\ge0$ in joules, define the admitted window\n$$\\Omega_{E_0,\\delta}:=\\{x\\in\\Omega:|E(x)-E_0|\\le\\delta\\}.$$\nWhen this set is nonempty, adopt the uniform preparation $P(x)=|\\Omega_{E_0,\\delta}|^{-1}$ on it and zero outside. Its dimensionless Boltzmann entropy is $\\log|\\Omega_{E_0,\\delta}|$, and its physical entropy convention is $k_{\\mathrm B}\\log|\\Omega_{E_0,\\delta}|$ in $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$. A zero-width window is allowed only when it contains at least one microstate.\n\nFor a continuous classical model, when the hypotheses and normalization in [[def-td-regular-hamiltonian-shell-preparation]] hold, the microcanonical preparation is the normalized shell measure $\\nu_{\\hat E}$ defined there. These finite-window and regular-shell rules are adopted model preparations. They do not assert Hamiltonian ergodicity, equality with long-time averages, canonical sampling, or equilibration.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "L1",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-hamiltonian-measure-and-recurrence",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $(M,\\omega)$ be a smooth $2n$-dimensional symplectic manifold and $H\\in C^\\infty(M,\\mathbb R)$, with Hamiltonian field defined by $\\iota_{X_H}\\omega=dH$. Wherever its local flow $\\phi_t$ is defined, it preserves the symplectic form and the volume measure $m$ determined by $\\omega^n/n!$. No completeness is asserted. For a region $R$ on which a nonzero-time map $T=\\phi_\\tau$ and all its iterates are defined, $T$ is a measure-preserving transformation. If $m(R)<\\infty$, then for every measurable $E\\subseteq R$, almost every point of $E$ returns to $E$ infinitely often under forward iteration.\n\nIf $m(R)=1$ and $T$ is ergodic, then for every $f\\in L^1(R,m)$ the averages $N^{-1}\\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}f(T^jx)$ converge almost everywhere and in $L^1$ to $\\int_Rf\\,dm$. Without ergodicity, the limit is the invariant conditional expectation supplied by Birkhoff's theorem, not necessarily the space mean. Finally, if each stated time map $\\phi_t$ is a diffeomorphism of a finite invariant region $R$, a density $p_0\\ge0$ with $\\int_Rp_0\\,dm=1$ and $\\int_R|p_0\\log p_0|\\,dm<\\infty$ transports by $p_t=p_0\\circ\\phi_{-t}$ with conserved fine-grained entropy $-k_B\\int_Rp_t\\log p_t\\,dm$, using $0\\log0=0$. Volume preservation alone does not imply ergodicity or a time-average/ensemble identity.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "L2",
          "source": "thm-tdmath-regular-energy-shell-measure",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. Let $O\\subset\\mathbb R^{2n}$ be open with its canonical symplectic form, let $H\\in C^2(O,\\mathbb R)$, and let $J\\subset\\mathbb R$ be open. Suppose $\\nabla H\\ne0$ on $H^{-1}(J)$ and $H^{-1}(K)$ is compact in $O$ for every compact $K\\subset J$. Define $\\mu_E$ by [[def-tdmath-regular-energy-shell]]. Then for every nonnegative Borel $f$ compactly supported in $H^{-1}(J)$,\n$$\\int_Of(x)\\,dx=\\int_J\\mu_E(f)\\,dE.$$\nFor every $E\\in J$ with nonempty shell $\\Sigma_E=H^{-1}(\\{E\\})$, $0<\\mu_E(1)<\\infty$, and $\\widehat\\mu_E=\\mu_E/\\mu_E(1)$ is a probability measure. Let $\\phi_t$ be a Hamiltonian flow map defined as a diffeomorphism on a full compact energy band containing $\\Sigma_E$ and preserving that band. Then $\\widehat\\mu_E$ is invariant under $\\phi_t$ for every such regular $E$. Critical levels and noncompact bands are outside this statement.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "By [F1] and [A2], the canonical Hamiltonian data, smoothness, and full-band invertible flow match the hypotheses of [L1]–[L2]. Energy is conserved along each flow line because $\\frac{d}{dt}\\hat H(\\phi_t(x))=d\\hat H(X_{\\hat H})=\\hat\\omega(X_{\\hat H},X_{\\hat H})=0$; the global-flow condition is an assumption, not a consequence of local equations.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "A1",
            "A2",
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "The draft suppliers [L1] and [L2] give volume preservation and shell-measure invariance for the matched model in step 1.1. Normalization by the positive finite shell mass preserves invariance, and [F2] assigns that normalized measure as the preparation. Hence $\\nu_{\\hat E}(\\phi_t^{-1}(A))=\\nu_{\\hat E}(A)$. This deduction remains conditional while both suppliers lack current Step 1 readiness.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "step 1.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Let a physical Hamiltonian model satisfy [[def-td-regular-hamiltonian-shell-preparation]] on a nonempty compact regular energy band, and adopt its normalized shell law by [[post-td-microcanonical-sampling]]. Boundary empty: The statement explicitly requires a nonempty state set, nonzero sector, nonempty shell, or positive trace; no empty-model conclusion is claimed.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Let a physical Hamiltonian model satisfy [[def-td-regular-hamiltonian-shell-preparation]] on a nonempty compact regular energy band, and adopt its normalized shell law by [[post-td-microcanonical-sampling]]. In addition to the definition's $C^2$ regularity, assume its numerical Hamiltonian $\\hat H$ is $C^\\infty$ and its Hamiltonian flow $\\phi_t$ is an invertible smooth map of the whole band for every $t\\in\\mathbb R$. Then, conditional on the current batch-12 draft mathematical interfaces [[thm-tdmath-hamiltonian-measure-and-recurrence]] and [[thm-tdmath-regular-energy-shell-measure]], every shell probability $\\nu_{\\hat E}$ is invariant:\n$$\\nu_{\\hat E}(\\phi_t^{-1}(A))=\\nu_{\\hat E}(A)$$\nfor every Borel set $A\\subseteq\\Sigma_{\\hat E}$ and every $t\\in\\mathbb R$. This result asserts no ergodicity, time-average equality, or thermalization.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "4d8e8d3bfaf79bcf24a56fbc2097133732e85a67e73e11da7c48ee0c66e8578c",
