          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume AC. Let $H$ be a self-adjoint quantum Hamiltonian bounded below with a complete discrete energy eigenfamily of finite multiplicity, and let $\\rho_0$ be any positive trace-class density operator of trace one. Let $\\hbar>0$ be the assigned action constant in $\\mathrm{J\\,s}$, adopt the unitary dynamics $U_t=e^{-itH/\\hbar}$ of [[post-nrqm-framework-autonomous-dynamics]], and assume the trace-class Gibbs and local moment conditions of [[pthm-td-general-quantum-canonical-identities]] that supply this discrete eigenfamily. Then, conditional on the current batch-12 draft theorem [[thm-tdmath-discrete-quantum-cesaro-dephasing]], the Cesaro state\n$$\\bar\\rho_\\tau:=\\frac1{\\tau}\\int_0^\\tau U_t\\rho_0U_t^*\\,dt$$\nconverges in trace norm as $\\tau\\to\\infty$ to $\\rho_{\\mathrm{diag}}=\\sum_E P_E\\rho_0P_E$, where $P_E$ is the spectral projection onto the full eigenspace of energy $E$. Coherences inside degenerate energy blocks remain. The limit need not be Gibbs, and no pointwise-in-time convergence or thermalization is asserted.",
